# Temperance marker — fix/463-lite-fixture-race
- date: 2026-11-05
- branch: fix/463-lite-fixture-race
- scope-decision: Right thing — give the dist/lite/ fixture one owner so
  `npm run build && npm test` stops failing 19 tests for a reason unrelated
  to the code. Right way — one vitest globalSetup that builds the fixture if
  absent, then delete the four copied self-heals. Simplest correct shape: the
  alternative, making the four self-heals mutually exclusive with a lock, adds
  machinery to preserve a pattern that should not exist.
- blast-radius: the four init-* test files plus vitest.config.ts. The setup
  never compiles src/, so a missing build still fails as a missing build —
  which is the objection vitest.config.ts records against globalSetup, and
  the reason the cure respects it rather than overriding it.
- verification: `npm run build && npm test` must reach 536 passed. Falsified
  if a DIFFERENT set of tests starts failing, which would mean the self-heals
  were load-bearing for something I have not found.
- reversible: yes — delete one file, revert one config line, restore four
  beforeEach blocks from git.
- drift-trigger: If this branch starts touching tests/harness/prepublish-bundle.test.ts,
  stop. That file drives the bundler as its own subject and must keep doing so.
